{
  "_comment": "Parity test actors for the local/ephemeral compose stack only (compose/scripts/init-env.sh --parity-fixtures). Layered onto the identity repo realm by the parity-fixtures-import service after realm-import; never imported anywhere else. Customer actors (customer, other-customer, customer-owner) are members of /customers (the group the customer service fine-grained admin permission covers, and parity-suite gets the same view/manage-members grant from parity-admin-permissions.json); staff actors are not. init-env renders it into .cache/parity/ and adds the realm LDAP federation as disabled (no OpenLDAP in compose). TPP-001 and TPP-002 are Keycloak-mode open-finance TPPs and parity-channel is a confidential stand-in for the first-party channel fintechbankx-mobile (all private_key_jwt, DPoP-bound, client credentials only): init-env generates one key pair each at runtime (private JWK only in .env); the renderer adds the public JWKS, copies audiences and scopes from the realm (of-tpp-conformance-template, fintechbankx-mobile), adds the fbx_client_type claim and defines the API scopes the realm lacks. The parity-psu-* scopes put a fixed customer_id (the PSU) into a client-credentials token when requested.",
  "realm": "fintechbankx",
